From: RicemanRhys <176650384+RicemanRhys@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 04:28:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Local-only: add xbox_bridge_resolve_handle accessor

Exposes the existing bridge_resolve_handle() handle-table lookup (already
used internally for NtClose etc.) to callers outside kernel_bridge.c, with
no change to what it does or to any other bridge behavior. Read-only,
does not consume or alter the handle table slot.

Added so a hand-written game-side routine (twoc's GetExitCodeThread
override) can resolve a guest handle token to the real native HANDLE
behind it, instead of going through ObReferenceObjectByHandle (which
this bridge always answers with a null object).

Local to this clone only, not raised upstream. See
'crash claude md/crash-recomp-reference-notes.md' in the outer repo,
section 18.9, for the twoc/-side rule this falls under and why.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/kernel/kernel_bridge.c      | 12 ++++++++++++
 src/kernel/xbox_memory_layout.h | 11 +++++++++++
 2 files changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/kernel/kernel_bridge.c b/src/kernel/kernel_bridge.c
index 5b56513..0f30f1f 100644
--- a/src/kernel/kernel_bridge.c
+++ b/src/kernel/kernel_bridge.c
@@ -2557,6 +2557,18 @@ static HANDLE bridge_resolve_handle(uint32_t token)
     return (HANDLE)(uintptr_t)token;
 }
 
+/* Public wrapper for bridge_resolve_handle (xbox_memory_layout.h). Additive:
+ * exposes this one existing lookup to callers outside this file, with no
+ * change to what it does or to any other bridge behavior. Added so a
+ * hand-written game-side routine (e.g. a title's GetExitCodeThread, which
+ * needs the real thread HANDLE, not another round trip through the bridge's
+ * own always-null ObReferenceObjectByHandle) can resolve a guest handle
+ * token without duplicating the handle table. */
+HANDLE xbox_bridge_resolve_handle(uint32_t token)
+{
+    return bridge_resolve_handle(token);
+}
+
 static HANDLE bridge_take_handle(uint32_t token)
 {
     if ((token & 0xFF000000u) == BRIDGE_HANDLE_TAG) {
diff --git a/src/kernel/xbox_memory_layout.h b/src/kernel/xbox_memory_layout.h
index 23df8b2..0098077 100644
--- a/src/kernel/xbox_memory_layout.h
+++ b/src/kernel/xbox_memory_layout.h
@@ -500,4 +500,15 @@ void  *xbox_thread_debug_handle(void); /* the game thread, or NULL under inline
 #define XBOX_THREAD_MODE_SPAWN  1
 void xbox_SetThreadMode(int mode);
 
+/* Resolve a bridge handle token (as stored in guest memory by
+ * bridge_write_handle -- CreateThread, CreateEvent, CreateFile, ...) back to
+ * the real native HANDLE behind it, for a hand-written game-side routine that
+ * needs the host object itself rather than another bridge call. Read-only:
+ * does not consume or alter the handle table slot (see bridge_resolve_handle
+ * in kernel_bridge.c, which this only exposes). An untagged/unknown token, or
+ * one with no live entry, returns NULL. Purely additive: no bridge behavior
+ * changes, this only makes an existing internal lookup reachable from
+ * outside kernel_bridge.c. */
+HANDLE xbox_bridge_resolve_handle(uint32_t token);
+
 #endif /* XBOX_MEMORY_LAYOUT_H */
